# Index Pages

When editing a module index page or its primitives, read:

- **`docs/05-index-pages.md`** — shared anatomy, per-module metric strips, group definitions, column specs, click flows
- **`docs/06-routing.md`** — how row clicks deep-link into the customer shell (`/customers/:customerId?tab=…&<id>=…`)
- **`docs/02-design-system.md`** — badge catalog, spacing
- **`docs/08-mock-data.md`** — seed records available to populate groups

## Key rules

1. Default landing = **All list** (flat table). **Focus** (grouped priority) is opt-in via toggle or `?view=groups`.
2. Groups show top 5 rows sorted by: urgency → value → date.
3. Same component handles both grouped and filtered list modes, toggled by `?group=…` query param.
4. Every row click navigates to the customer shell with the right tab + record ID.
5. Sidebar items point to **index routes**, not hardcoded record IDs.
